The Northbridge NDA defines "Confidential Information" as all information disclosed by a Party to the other in connection with the Purpose, in any form, that is marked confidential or would reasonably be understood to be confidential [1].

The definition of Confidential Information excludes:
- Information that becomes public other than through a breach of the Agreement [1];
- Information that was lawfully known to the Recipient before disclosure [1];
- Information that is independently developed without use of the Discloser's information [1].
